@@ -9,6 +9,19 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## View preservation
+
+Client navigation retains up to five content views, including the active view, in a
+persistent Astro container. Returning to a cached pathname and query string reuses
+the existing DOM and hydrated islands. Inactive views use `content-visibility:
+hidden` and `inert`; browsers without content visibility use `display: none`.
+The least recently used view is removed when the limit is exceeded.
+
+Astro still fetches the destination for current head metadata and shell content.
+Cached content keeps its client state until eviction or a full reload. Navigating
+to the same URL refreshes that view. Sign-in and sign-up use `cacheView={false}`
+on the shared layout so their form contents are discarded when leaving.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
